<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#greek-fire">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greek fire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greek fire was an incendiary weapon used by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, typically projected from siphons on warships, and able to burn on water. Its exact composition was a closely guarded secret and remains uncertain. It played an important part in Byzantine naval defence, notably against Arab fleets of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> during the sieges of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greek-fire.jpg" alt="Greek fire" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greekfire-madridskylitzes1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
